The first local run exposed a certificate-encoding issue—not a theorem failure. A plain permutation cannot record the proof’s third pivot when that index is retained for later recursion, so the generic constructive algorithm could not round-trip through the certificate language. I’m correcting the witness to the faithful bounded object: a list of `(minimum endpoint, row-maximum partner, retained minimum neighbor)` triples plus the final 4/5-index base case. It remains under the 256-atom cap.
